No!  Keep it in; as long as it only happens when using shift or control
movements, it is highly beneficial.  While the epitome of bad luck is to
rush down a hall onto a dead cockatrice, it can be irritating to land on
ghost hordes with pickup on, knowing that everything is going to be cursed.

Some other thoughts:

1) Succubi should not be able to seduce you during prayer.
2) Monsters should leave corpses a bit more regularly.
3) When you dedicate an altar to your god, it should increase your
    favor with him.  Occasionally, on encountering an altar on the
    first level, characters of mine have died sacrificing food on
    chaotic altars (wizards all, and therefore neutral), only to
    have corpse production suddenly stop, and, of course, Thoth 
    is rather angry about all that sacrificing "to" Anhur.  This 
    behavior should at the very least change when the altar is 
    finally rededicated.
4) One should be able to select one's own alignment.  There doesn't
    seem to be enough of a difference to unbalance the game in so
    doing. 
5) As far as unbalancing the game, there should be an "enchant object"
   scroll.  Very rare, of course, but it would turn a tin of jackal meat
   into spinach (strange are the ways of magic), a pair of boots into 
   levitation boots, or if you're unlucky, fumbling, or if you're lucky,
   speed boots; name a weapon (some limits would have to be put here).
   With this, there is no longer the arbitrary division into items that 
   are enchantable by a spell and those that are "one-of-a-kind" (which
   is a pretty weak justification, given the tendency they have to  
   accumulate once you have that crucial first one), or made out-of-dungeon.
6) There no longer seems to be much in the way of correlation between monster
    abilities and resistances (see .sig), -- whatever happened to the old
    "eat a killer bee, get poison resistance" motif?
7) Pet snakes shouldn't hide under items.  This is merely an idle wish, since
    they have my nomination for "worst pet" but could be passable if this 
    were fixed.  Regarding unusual monster abilities, there should probably
    be a limit as to how often a piercer player can plummet from the ceiling
    onto the heads of suspecting monsters (after you've fallen on even a jackal
    twice, it's not likely to let you jump to the ceiling.  How DO piercers
    get back up on the ceiling, anyway?
8) One should never encounter a bus error when falling through a trap door
    from a shop (bad move, right there -- but there were no unpaid items!)
    onto a ghost level with a ring of regeneration, a +7 athame, and a 
    posthumously identified wand of wishing.  Never.  Under any circumstances.

